  "non_claims": [
    "PKSMP5 qualifies exactly one frozen four-vCPU QEMU topology with BSP 0 and legacy-xAPIC APs 1, 2, and 3; it is not a general topology, hotplug, NUMA, multi-socket, or x2APIC implementation.",
    "The capability token remains a fixed development value and is not a production minting, delegation, revocation, or secrecy mechanism.",
    "Each AP invalidates exactly one frozen probe page in its private root for one generation; address-space-wide invalidation, concurrent generations, INVPCID, PCID, and broadcast shorthand remain open.",
    "The aggregate mask is assembled from three separately validated private mailbox acknowledgements; no shared writable mailbox or arbitrary remote callback is introduced.",
    "No scheduler, task migration, CPU affinity authority, user task, service, driver, PGVM2, PDC, or PooleGlyph workload is dispatched.",
    "The injected APIC-4 timeout proves one partial-start rollback point, not every hardware or timing failure interleaving.",
    "QEMU TCG evidence is not physical-target evidence and does not close N8, N9, or production qualification.",
    "The retained Cycle 140 PKSMP4 receipt remains historical evidence for the predecessor one-AP slice; PKSMP5 does not rewrite that receipt.",
    "No signature, authority grant, authorized action, production promotion, firmware mutation, or physical-media write occurs."
